<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- agent-infra-plist-version: 0.1.0 -->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- worktree reaper (#1095, armed via #1311): a daily pass over the
         tortoise repo's worktrees. The reaper itself is
         agent-infra/scripts/pi-reap-worktrees.sh, and it is FARMED to
         {{HOME}}/.pi/agent/scripts/ by pi-bootstrap/setup.sh's fleet-scripts
         farm — that copy is what this template targets, and it is not
         optional: launchd cannot read a script under ~/Documents, because
         macOS TCC is per-binary and denies a launchd-spawned `bash` the read
         ("Operation not permitted") and a launchd-spawned `git` the repo read
         ("not a git repository"). Running the script from ~/.pi/agent/scripts
         is the whole fix (#427), the same mechanism the pi-session-reaper
         above already relies on.

         SHIPS IN DRY-RUN (the `dry_run` flag below): this job deletes
         worktrees and branches it classifies as provably dead, so arming it
         live is a deliberate, per-machine operator decision, not a default.
         Flip it by removing that flag HERE and re-running
         scripts/install-launchd.sh.

         The pass is bounded by REAP_WT_BUDGET_SECONDS (default 300s); a pass
         that exhausts it defers the remainder and reports DEFERRED rather than
         removing anything unclassified. A dry-run pass on the live estate
         reported REMOVE=0 DEFERRED=432 of 454 worktrees, so this job's present
         effect is a report, not a removal, and the budget (agent-infra #1095)
         is the lever that decides how much one pass can classify.

         The `repo` argument is {{TORTOISE_REPO}} because the reaper takes the
         repo to operate on. A machine without a tortoise checkout leaves that
         placeholder unresolved, and install-launchd.sh then SKIPS this
         template by design (unresolved placeholder) instead of installing a
         broken target.

         No StandardOutPath/StandardErrorPath: every pass writes its own capped
         log at ~/.pi/agent/state/pi-reap-worktrees.log (an unbounded
         launchd-captured log is the twin of the symlink-truncation surface the
         reaper already guards). -->
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.tortoise.worktree-reaper</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/usr/bin/env</string>
        <string>bash</string>
        <string>{{HOME}}/.pi/agent/scripts/pi-reap-worktrees.sh</string>
        <string>--repo</string>
        <string>{{TORTOISE_REPO}}</string>
        <string>--dry-run</string>
    </array>
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>{{PATH}}</string>
    </dict>
    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>86400</integer>
</dict>
</plist>
